      "content": "the \"fabric of time being torn asunder\"... that's exactly how it feels watching it. it's heavy. \n\nokay, let's try to test this. i was looking back at the notes from earlier. that jittery, violent movement at 2:14 PM... i looked up what happened at that time in different years. i found out that at 2:14 PM on April 15, 1912, the Titanic was actually below the water line after the collision. and then there was that sudden, sharp spike in the pendulum's movement at 8:46 AM today... i'm not sure what that corresponds to yet, but it felt so jarring. \n\nif this clock is actually \"recording\" these things, how deep does it go? could it be reacting to things that haven't even happened yet, or is it strictly a record of the past? and is there a way to tell if a specific movement refers to a person or a whole era?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
